{
  "scene": "review",
  "expected": "Next, we run the AI-assisted bid review. We include every admitted bidder, confirm consent, and review their submissions against the issued criteria. The review is read only. Here, you can see both bidders compared against the same requirements. When the documents don't establish a required reference contract or a committed delivery plan, the result says, not evidenced. It doesn't fill in the gap. Instead, it gives the committee specific questions to follow up. Can we verify these references? Are the delivery milestones clear? Does the price build-up support the proposal? That is where the AI helps: it prepares a clearer review, so people can spend their time checking what matters.",
